Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 18:11:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 114/116] =?UTF-8?q?ChopGimp:=20expressions=20in=20the=20co?=
 =?UTF-8?q?mpact=20value=20fields,=20behind=20effects=20in=20previews,=20s?=
 =?UTF-8?q?troke=20=C2=AB=20Aligner=20sur=20le=20calque=20=C2=BB?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- options bar value field (chopgimp-value-field.c): typed text goes
  through GimpEevl (gimp_eevl_evaluate(), as GimpSpinButton /
  GimpSizeEntry): "2*5", "50+10", "100/3", "(1+2)*3"; the field's unit
  ("51 px", "50 %") and px/pt are accepted and ignored; falls back to
  the plain number parse
- behind effects (drop shadow / outer glow in a blend mode) in layer
  thumbnails and gimp_drawable_get_buffer_with_effects(): composited
  normal under the filtered drawable, as Photoshop's thumbnails
  (chopgimp_behind_effects_get_preview_source(): gegl:over chain kept
  per layer, rebuilt when the behind effects change; used by the reduced
  preview copy and the validate buffer). The canvas is unchanged.
- chopgimp:stroke "align-with-layer" (default on = rendering of before):
  off, the gradient spans the image canvas and the pattern starts at the
  canvas origin. The canvas in layer coordinates is given by
  GimpDrawableFilter (gimp_operation_contour_set_canvas()) at creation,
  on layer offset changes and image size changes; only a non-aligned
  gradient/pattern stroke is rendered again (fused styles notified).
  XCF fx cache key: the property left out at its default (old keys
  valid), canvas added when off. Stroke dialog: « Aligner sur le
  calque » (gradient), « Lier au calque » (pattern).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
